+# Polygon historical successful-output recovery
+
+Request `d3e02609-794e-4a8b-b934-11f92bd57817`. This is the separate Polygon output, not a transfer or repeat of Task3/a63 ownership. No platform implementation, binary replacement, installation or restart is required. Future automatic capture is already installed separately under 806cdc24; this package does not modify it.
+
+## Evidence and scope
+
+Original task `eb68d953-2ec5-4aa9-8b12-e3004784c31d`, session `c34cbefe-12a4-44cf-8ea9-a138b52d436c`, workspace `25f53734-5aea-490e-b7ba-d5da6fe821dd`. Protected claim and saved-model envelopes bind root and project directory `/data/tasks/feature-8227-importa_gim9c2mm`, project `kd_8227_pair366`. Service is `app_base`; output is `kd_8227_pair366_app_base:php84-366r10`.
+
+The exact authorized receipt SHA256 is `6489014ba72579758b5f7305bd910e4d1544515b8b4479582fca05165120108d`. It identifies `co-up/.kandev/pair-366/build.stdout-stderr.log` (807202 bytes, SHA256 `b957e78d6abb28ace5f5d961e7b9b9f055972cf7ccde8303086b4ee40dc4dfa2`). Neither owner artifact is treated as independent success/ID proof. No source, package, full image metadata, environment, command, credential or task-data contents were exported.
+
+A bounded stat-only discovery of the existing default-node client reference index found exactly one file within the supplied build interval. Only that candidate's metadata was read; its exact task-root path component and target matched. It supplies native Ref `qzlhr9rvyz88fysq969f52dp2`, builder/node `default/default`. This is a discovery pointer, not terminal proof. No native history list, task census or foreign build record was requested.
+
+The existing audited native reader then queried only that Ref. Native created time is `2026-11-25T23:30:27.081324747Z`; terminal completion is `2026-11-25T23:33:16.030655963Z`. Event type 1, no error or external error, exactly one image exporter named `docker.io/library/kd_8227_pair366_app_base:php84-366r10`. See `native-output-proof.json`. The reader verifies result-linked content SHA/size and projects only index/manifest descriptors; it does not read config/layer/provenance/log blobs.
+
+| Role | Independently verified digest |
+| --- | --- |
+| Native result/exporter target, OCI index | `sha256:b341fecdb97d66942f1eb3501343760ffdb1e26e9c77a603eca31354fd3bd137` |
+| Selected linux/amd64 platform manifest | `sha256:6093688504ec36bb3b8b33a6c2c7729fa2f3812b1b6b6a1fa978fe3ef7c25d5e` |
+| Config descriptor, not config content | `sha256:0029ce02a40cdab570e49e81d4cd0cf04b57e4806f806b6dbd633b230a6c93f1` |
+
+The attestation pointer from the owner log was not used or fetched. No current engine `.Id` or RepoDigest was observed by Support. The migration's required `image_id` is a **native completed output target equality predicate**, explicitly annotated `engine_id_observed: false`; it is not a claim that index, platform and config digests are interchangeable. The installed reader must independently resolve the scoped tag and match its literal `.Id` to that predicate during Root's separate owner acceptance. Any mismatch fails closed; no config/ID/tag fallback is authorized.
+
+## Exact migration and compatibility
+
+`restore-known-output.py` is a new fixed-scope adaptation of the admitted a63/pass2 migration. It never runs the a63 migration or accesses Task3's receipt. It pins Ref, native timestamps, exporter, output chain, project, root/clone and tag. The production entry also pins the exact protected claim/model hashes and all five installed broker/module/wrapper/client/guard hashes. A model reference or build intent supplies no output proof.
+
+Only one protected v1 receipt may be created. Existing target/symlink fails without replacement; publication uses a 0600 fsynced temporary file and atomic no-replace hard link, then fsyncs the directory. It retains broker UID/GID and checks claim/model byte equality before and after. No claim/model/resource is rewritten. A repeat is rejected, preserving the existing receipt. `reviewed.json` pins migration and native-proof bytes for the reviewed host launcher. This is not an agent-facing receipt import endpoint.
+
+Installed reader/module SHA256 is `1f075423e4c89e32caa359e2b27e12086aad4d0adc1f5e4eafe54052a1e7608a`, from deployment implementation `c4f5b4ec1574abe1a24c4287dd356154a6b3d61c` and installed evidence `6ab463cb0c4ba5af8490c9ec928cd726ac8c56f2`. Broker is unchanged `9514b692d9833fcc64c1978b7553c181c37e84625e645a0ad0521d4b2f298e91`. Fresh complete dependency hashes are in `installed-before.json`. Existing image, lifecycle, volume, task-access and completion-capture code remains untouched.
+
+Validation is distinct from affected-owner acceptance:
+
+- 16 native-reader source tests pass offline.
+- 18 migration/reader cases run in private fixtures against installed code, including root-to-UID1000 custody, foreign task/clone, changed snapshot, symlink, repeat, malformed/nonterminal/failed proof and output-digest discrimination.
+- 18 installed image-boundary cases use the real wrapper/client transport with a mocked engine and private synthetic credentials. No live broker identity, image or workload is queried.
+- Source migration run passes its applicable cases; root-custody case runs in the installed root fixture rather than being counted as source acceptance.
+
+## Separately bound original-owner acceptance
+
+Root may bind **one** curated tag inspection in original session `c34cbefe-12a4-44cf-8ea9-a138b52d436c`, unchanged task root/project/caller and existing restricted environment:
+
+```sh
+KANDEV_TASK_DOCKER_ACCESS=restricted docker image inspect kd_8227_pair366_app_base:php84-366r10
+```
+
+Run from the exact registered project directory `/data/tasks/feature-8227-importa_gim9c2mm`. Preserve stdout/stderr/exit and compare curated `Id` literally with the native target above. Success establishes actual engine `.Id` equality at that owner operation; synthetic tests and historical recovery do not. On denial/mismatch, stop and preserve evidence; no second inspection, ID fallback, model registration, tag mutation or build is authorized by this package. No paired test or source/vendor qualification follows automatically.
+
+The protected metadata result is recorded in `restoration.json` after the reviewed apply. No binary rollback is applicable because no implementation was changed. The operation never overwrites an earlier receipt; any later reversal of this exact appended receipt would require a separately scoped, hash-bound metadata action. All real images, worktrees, databases, networks and logs remain untouched.
diff --git a/docs/polygon-build-receipt-d3e02609/apply-restoration.py b/docs/polygon-build-receipt-d3e02609/apply-restoration.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3092248
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/polygon-build-receipt-d3e02609/apply-restoration.py
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Reviewed host launcher, not a task-facing command or installed capability."""
+import hashlib
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+import subprocess
+
+HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+review = json.loads((HERE/'reviewed.json').read_bytes())
+source = (HERE/'restore-known-output.py').read_bytes()
+proof = (HERE/'native-output-proof.json').read_bytes()
+assert hashlib.sha256(source).hexdigest() == review['restore_sha256']
+assert hashlib.sha256(proof).hexdigest() == review['proof_sha256']
+repo = HERE.parents[1]
+assert subprocess.run(['git','branch','--show-current'],cwd=repo,capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip() == 'main'
+def identity():
+    return subprocess.run(['docker','inspect','kandev','--format','{{.Id}} {{.Image}} {{.State.StartedAt}} {{.RestartCount}}'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip()
+before = identity()
+result = subprocess.run(['docker','exec','-i','--user','0',before.split()[0],'/usr/bin/python3','-I','-B','-c',source.decode(),'--apply'],input=json.dumps(review).encode()+b'\n'+proof,capture_output=True)
+(HERE/'restoration-attempt.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(returncode=result.returncode,stdout=result.stdout.decode(),stderr=result.stderr.decode()),indent=2)+'\n')
+if result.returncode:
+    raise SystemExit(result.stderr.decode())
+receipt=json.loads(result.stdout)
+after=identity(); receipt.update(container_identity_before=before,container_identity_after=after,unchanged_container=before==after,restart=False)
+(HERE/'restoration.json').write_text(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2)+'\n')
+assert before==after
+print(json.dumps(receipt,indent=2))
